# BioBand Core Rules

## Stack
- Expo managed workflow (Expo Go first)
- TypeScript strict mode
- React Navigation (bottom tabs)
- i18next for all UI strings (tr + en)
- Dark theme via `src/theme/colors.ts`

## Development Workflow
- Build in small, testable phases; one feature at a time
- Ask the user before assuming on unclear requirements
- Warn before requiring native modules or expo-dev-client
- Explain decisions briefly — this is a learning project

## Code Style
- Functional components only
- No hardcoded UI strings — use `useTranslation()` and locale JSON files
- Reuse existing components and theme tokens
- Keep comments short and in English; explain non-obvious logic only

## File Organization
```
src/
  components/   # Shared UI
  screens/      # Screen components
  navigation/   # Navigators
  i18n/         # Translations
  theme/        # Colors and shared styles
  types/        # TypeScript types
```

## Expo Go Compatibility
- Prefer packages that work in Expo Go
- Use `expo-audio` (not `expo-av`) for audio features
- Use event-based recording for multi-track (not microphone capture)
